# Python bytecode caches. Regenerated on every run of tools/*.py, so tracking
# them means a spurious binary diff after each preflight.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# OS and editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp

# Customer PII must never enter this repo. Lead and policy exports are read
# from Dropbox at runtime and stay there.
leads-master.csv
policies-master.csv
*-leads-*.csv

# Scratch files from ad-hoc curl/verification runs. These get written to the
# repo root whenever a shell lands here instead of the scratchpad directory,
# which happened during the 7 Aug statewide flip. They are never project content.
*.tmp
*.html.bak
urls*.txt

# Credentials. Added 13 Aug 2026, before any key existed, because the Search
# Console API is OAuth-only and the setup for it involves a service account JSON
# key — and an external agent's instructions for that setup said to "drop the JSON
# key somewhere on the machine Claude Code runs on", which here means the repo.
#
# A GCP service account private key committed to GitHub is a live, NON-EXPIRING
# credential in permanent history; rotating it later does not remove it. As of
# today there are already five plaintext credential stores in synced Dropbox
# (OPEN-ITEMS.md Tier 1), so the failure mode is demonstrated, not theoretical.
#
# tools/gsc-pull.py also refuses to run against a key inside this repo. Two
# mechanisms, because either alone depends on somebody remembering.
*-credentials.json
*-credential.json
gcp-*.json
*service-account*.json
*service_account*.json
gsc-sa*.json
client_secret*.json
*.pem
*.p12
*.key
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── BORDEREAUX AND ANYTHING PER-POLICY ────────────────────────────────────
# The carrier bordereaux carry `Insured (Full Name)` and `Street Address` for
# every policy the agency has written. Only aggregates may be committed. The
# per-carrier breakdown is excluded separately: it contains no personal data,
# but carrier-level pricing is not ours to publish.
*BDX*.xlsx
*bordereaux*.xlsx
internal-carrier-check.json
premium-aggregates/**/internal-*.json
